WEBVTT

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
REUNION

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.820
Yo. Nice to meet you.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.900
Oh, hi there.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.030
Even Tsukasa is here?

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:00.320
Satoru...

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.290
does your peak have a rainbow?

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.460
My peak doesn't.

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:10.330
I hate bugs so there aren't
any butterflies either.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.460
What about yours, Satoru?

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.840
I don't believe it. You don't mean...?

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.340
Mr. Hayashi.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:20.720
He shared his peak with both of us.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:24.010
You've never said
anything about that before...

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.850
I'd promised him I wouldn't tell you until
you said you wanted to be an employee.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.190
Both Mr. Hayashi and I decided to join
the Company of our own free will,

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.730
so we didn't want you to feel coerced.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.650
You and Mr. Hayashi are both employees?

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:43.410
This is weird. Why isn't Mr. Hayashi
telling me this himself?

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.330
Mr. Hayashi has come back, right?

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.620
He has. He's in the next room.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:00.970
Mr. Hayashi!

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:07.890
Mr. Hayashi...?

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.400
What on earth happened to you...?

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:16.780
Mr. Hayashi!

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:24.700
There's nothing left...
He's been completely crushed.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.790
Crushed...?

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.330
What are you saying?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.420
Why would Mr. Hayashi get crushed?!
What're you talking about, Tsukasa?

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:39.050
Tell me what's going on!
Tell me now!

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.930
Hiroki did it...

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.430
Hiroki was the one
who crushed Mr. Hayashi.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:53.190
Aren't you hamming it up
 a bit too much, Tsukasa?

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.810
That was supposed to be your line.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.820
Hiroki? Why?

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.820
Meiling...

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.080
Tell me exactly what's going on here!

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:10.250
She also has an image.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.960
But she was raised differently to us.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.960
Just take a look at her peak
and you'll see.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.460
Meiling's peak giver was Mr. Hayashi.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:28.470
What's happened to her peak...?

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:37.480
It's like her valley has encroached
upon her peak...

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.280
Meiling, it's nice to meet you.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:45.700
Um...

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:48.030
The "bigeon" hates cats!

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.580
Mister told me you'd come...

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.540
Meiling, you need to look
at the butterfly.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.920
Otherwise the valley will get bigger.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:06.760
Mr. Hayashi didn't let this child
have a lock.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.760
She has no lock? Why?

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:14.270
Having no lock means she can sync up
to a target without touching them.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.690
Besides, it eliminated
the hassle of creating a lock,

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.570
which made her usable
from the moment she was given a peak.

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:25.070
Indeed, Meiling here has already completed
several frontline assignments.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.280
That's not the point.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.790
I want to know why Mr. Hayashi
would make her without a lock!

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.460
The first thing I was taught was
how to create a lock.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:39.250
Mr. Hayashi knows better than anyone
the dangers of not having a lock.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:42.670
It's unthinkable that he'd have her
do jobs without one!

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.510
If her valley keeps
eroding her peak like this,

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.510
there'll be no place left
to sit down peacefully like that.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.720
Hiroki said the same thing, you know.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:55.810
And then used it as a reason
to crush Mr. Hayashi.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:01.360
Hiroki crushed Mr. Hayashi
to uphold his own idea of justice!

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:06.190
Compassion is more important than
a sense of justice, am I right?

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.320
Can we finish this conversation "outside"?

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:12.450
Discussing this stuff here
is going to upset Meiling.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:15.500
You're right. Let's leave, Satoru.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:19.620
See you later, Meiling.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.840
Meiling, are you listening?

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:29.470
If a man with a scar here
ever comes to visit you,

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.600
I want you to tell him in secret.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.640
Tell him one of my carrier pigeons
is flying around.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:35.850
A "bigeon"?

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.850
No, a "pigeon".
A carrier pigeon who hates cats.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:43.730
A "carry-a-bigeon"...?

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:47.900
Satoru.

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:50.570
There's no point.
The old Mr. Hayashi is gone.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:56.950
You haven't answered
my question yet, Tsukasa.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.330
The Mr. Hayashi I knew

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:02.710
would never have left a kid
without a lock.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.880
You'd better give me a good explanation!

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:11.050
There's no way his views would've flipped
in the two years since I saw him!

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.050
I hadn't seen him either.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:18.270
I hadn't seen Mr. Hayashi
for over 12 years.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:19.560
12 years?

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:22.810
That's right.
Tsukasa had Hiroki under his wing.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:24.980
And Hayashi had you.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:29.950
Both of them were so busy that they
didn't even have time to meet until today.

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:33.070
So that's why he got so upset...

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:35.200
Wait...

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:39.120
So it wasn't Mr. Hayashi that
brought Meiling here?

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:42.830
I was the one to bring Meiling to Tsukasa.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.090
Hayashi was hospitalized
the moment he got back.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:52.590
His ulcers got worse than ever,
so he wasn't able to care for Meiling.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:53.470
Care?

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:58.430
Mr. Hayashi had come back to ask me
to take care of Meiling.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:03.230
If she were in my peak, she wouldn't
have to constantly look at her butterfly.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.110
She might even be able to play.

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:08.900
Mr. Hayashi thought if she was cared for,
it would all be okay.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:10.610
So he made her without a lock.

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:12.860
"Okay"?

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:16.120
Just what is "okay" about someone
needing care forever?

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:21.790
I guess he thought it was possible
as he'd cared for my mother too.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.830
Something here's giving me the creeps.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:29.380
Mr. Hayashi's experience must've made him
think a child without a lock was feasible.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:33.720
I don't think it's as out of character
as you seem to think, Satoru.

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:36.890
All their answers seem kind of vague.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.850
There's nothing out of character
about it at all!

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:42.640
It was Hayashi who said he wouldn't
give her a lock!

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:46.900
That's it! It's only Mr. Katsuragi.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:50.900
He's the only one saying he heard it
from Mr. Hayashi directly.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:55.320
So you heard nothing from Mr. Hayashi?

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:57.700
This stuff about Meiling.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.910
Mr. Hayashi didn't tell you about it,
even over the phone?

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:04.540
No, I got the information
from Mr. Katsuragi.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.790
So Mr. Katsuragi is your only source?

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.960
Hey! What's with the third degree, Satoru?

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:15.220
I just can't believe that Mr. Hayashi
would choose not to give her a lock.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.970
I lived with him for a long time.

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:22.020
I know Mr. Hayashi the best
out of all of us!

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:26.270
So, your report alone isn't enough
to convince me.

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:29.190
There must have been something else.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:31.190
Something, like what?

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:34.110
There might've been some circumstances

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:37.200
that forced Mr. Hayashi
to leave her without a lock.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:39.820
You don't believe what I said then?

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:43.200
So you think Mr. Hayashi was coerced
into creating Meiling?

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.410
Tsukasa...

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:49.040
can we really believe what
Mr. Katsuragi is saying here?

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:53.250
Mr. Katsuragi, would you show us
your memories, please?

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:54.340
What?

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:58.840
Mr. Hayashi spoke to you about making
a child without a lock, didn't he?

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:01.930
So, you must have a memory
of that conversation.

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:06.640
Please show us. If Satoru is this
concerned, perhaps I should be too.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:10.730
Show them Katsuragi.
It won't cost you anything.

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:14.320
Damn you and your trust issues, Satoru!

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.030
What about you, Satoru?

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:17.360
I'm going in too.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:29.790
I'm planning not to give Meiling a lock.

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:34.210
That way, you lot will become able
to manipulate people's memories too.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:39.630
You'll be able to enter people's loci
by making use of Meiling's image.

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:43.640
Won't not having a lock cause her
problems down the road?

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:48.390
She'll probably be unable to live
a regular life. I'll take care of her.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:53.690
If we go down this road, Meiling will live
her life not knowing what reality is.

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:56.820
But she won't suffer
from a guilty conscience either.

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:59.070
It'll be easier for her long-term.

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:01.990
Besides...

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:05.410
I don't want Satoru to have to
do too much dirty work.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:11.210
He made Meiling to protect you, Satoru.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:13.290
I told Hiroki...

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:17.710
I told him that my peak giver
was Mr. Hayashi.

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:24.050
He knew Mr. Hayashi was our peak giver
but still went ahead and crushed him!

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:25.890
That's right.

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:29.060
Hiroki made himself
the arbiter of justice.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:35.190
Damn...
 You're one scary dude, Tsukasa.

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:40.070
Satoru's the suspicious type, you know.

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:43.200
He won't just swallow
whatever we tell him.

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:45.990
Then let's use that to our advantage.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:49.580
Let him have his suspicions,
then present proof that he's wrong.

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:50.580
What proof?

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:53.210
We'll change Katsuragi's memories a bit.

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:54.170
What?

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:56.250
A switcheroo.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:59.090
In your memory of the time
I suggested making "babies",

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:02.090
we'll make it so Hayashi was
the one who suggested it.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.680
We'll alter the script a little too.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:10.730
I'm home.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.600
What time do you call this?

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:18.230
Who's that?

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:19.440
Huh?

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:24.200
The kid sitting next to Boo's cage.
I don't think we've met.

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:30.830
Don't say creepy stuff like that!
You know I'm here alone at night.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.750
But someone's right there!

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:35.540
There's nobody here.
Stop trying to scare me!

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.960
There's nobody here.
Stop trying to scare me!

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:39.000
What the hell...?

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:42.010
-What's that supposed to mean?
-What's that supposed to mean?

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:44.380
Why're you copying her?

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.550
Oh, do you mean the mirror?

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:49.640
I am a mirror.

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:54.640
I'm just a reflection is all.
There's nothing to worry about.

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:01.150
I see, it's just a mirror.
That must be it.

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.150
Stop worrying, will you?

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:07.280
What do I do now?

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:11.950
Oh yeah, wake me up with
a phone call later, okay?

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:14.710
What's the point in
living together like this?

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.210
-There's no point in my being here.
-I come home...

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:18.920
...and you're already at work.

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:22.920
Then you come home when
I'm about to leave for work.

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:24.130
If you cut your hours...

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:27.340
But, what can I possibly do?

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:35.140
I won't forgive Hiroki.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:37.690
I'll never forgive him for this.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:39.900
Neither will I.

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:43.650
We'll find Hiroki together
and change his memories.

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:45.450
Change his memories?

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:49.450
We'll crush him to bits!
Just like he's done to Mr. Hayashi!

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:52.830
Stay calm, Satoru.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:56.960
If you crush him, he'll have no idea
what's being done to him.

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.210
Wouldn't that be letting him off too easy?

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:03.760
Personally, I think we ought to change his
memories so that he spends his life

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.970
atoning for his crime, don't you?

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:08.800
Yeah, that's good.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:14.470
Because after all, our goal is to get
you guys to make us a perfect pet.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:17.980
Okay, the rest is up to you, Tsukasa.

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:22.070
I'll brief Satoru right now.
We already have a plan worked out.

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:25.070
If we can get just one perfect pet,

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:28.320
the rest of the rabble
 can go in the trash.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:33.280
As you know, Hiroki is able
to kick people out of memory loci.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:36.250
If he does that to us, it's game over.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:40.290
So before that happens we'll use your door
to move to another locus.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.170
You're the fastest among us.

00:14:43.630 --> 00:14:45.300
But sometimes my door...

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:47.470
Doesn't open, right?

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:49.470
Only in front of a valley.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:54.060
Listen, Satoru. That only happens
when you know what's on the other side.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:59.190
Knowing there's a valley waiting for you
is what makes your door jam.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:01.730
What he means is that
you chicken out.

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:03.230
There's another thing, though.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:06.320
Your door has grown lately, right?

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:07.610
Grown?

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:10.200
Has it been that size
since you were a kid?

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:12.570
It was from an anime originally, no?

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:15.200
An anime? Which one?

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:18.200
They aired it in China too, Jin.

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:21.210
You're right... It was smaller.

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:25.840
Without even realizing it,
you've modified your image over time.

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:30.340
Even how it jams is related
to your personal emotions.

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:35.140
In other words, it is highly adaptable.

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:38.600
So you should be able to do more with it
than you have been.

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:41.730
Damn, Tsukasa picks up on so much.

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:44.980
Listen, Satoru. We need you
to modify your door, okay?

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:49.690
Your door will be crucial for us
to be able to change Hiroki's memories.

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:51.490
One other thing...

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:54.490
Can we entrust you with Meiling's care?

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:58.910
You've never done it before so it might
be best for you to get used to it.

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:01.250
Sure, no problem.

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:04.000
I just need to bring her
into my peak, right?

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:07.420
Right. Go ahead and use that guest room.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.010
You can lock the door too.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:10.340
Understood.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:21.230
You sure it's okay
to leave those two alone?

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:23.770
I'd be more worried
if they weren't alone.

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:26.980
He's taking Meiling into
his peak, don't forget.

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:29.570
If anyone were to sync
with Meiling then...

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:31.570
That's not the point though, is it!

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:34.820
We don't know what Hayashi said to her!

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:37.530
What if Satoru starts
asking her questions?

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:40.240
Oh right... That'd be bad.

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:43.540
You need a break or something?
You're starting to drop the ball!

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.080
Give me the spare key, Long.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:48.040
I'll go tell him to stop.

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:50.340
Hi.

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:53.590
I remembered! It's a "carry-a-bigeon"!

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:56.010
Mister said to tell you
there's a "carry-a-bigeon".

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:57.680
A "carry-a-bigeon"?

00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:01.470
Is the "mister" you're talking about
Mr. Hayashi?

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:04.810
Oh, she means a carrier pigeon...

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:09.980
This isn't Meiling's house...

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:12.690
No, it isn't. You're in my home now.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:17.820
Tsukasa!

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:20.830
Fascinating, there are two rainbows...

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:26.370
What do you think you're doing?

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:29.960
You didn't have to jump out like that.
I wasn't going to do anything.

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:32.840
And now we're even too.

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:36.930
You'll be entering my peak as well,

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:39.350
when we change Hiroki's memories.

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:42.390
It's part of the plan to make sure
he doesn't escape.

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:43.600
Part of the plan?

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:46.440
That's when I'll use my back door trick.

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:48.100
You'll see when the time comes.

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:50.980
And that trick will enable me
to crush you.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.570
Anyway, Long is calling for you.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:55.610
I'll take over from here.

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:57.700
Okay. See you later then.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:01.490
You think I'd make Hiroki believe
his peak giver was the CEO?

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:05.790
Doing something like that would put me
 at a serious disadvantage.

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:09.080
We'll dive in as if to change
Hiroki's memories,

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:12.420
but it's going to end with you
getting crushed, Satoru.

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:14.670
"It was an accident, sir..."

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:18.260
"Hiroki was too powerful
for Satoru after all."

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:21.260
"What would you like to do now, sir?"

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:25.350
"Looks like I'm the only usable pet
you have left."

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:35.230
Tsukasa, I'll take over.

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.780
You should get some rest.

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.780
I'd rather you went and got changed.

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:44.660
We'll go look for Hiroki
as soon as you're ready.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.910
Understood. I'll go wake up Mr. Katsuragi.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:50.710
Once Satoru is out of the picture

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:53.540
and I'm the only usable pet left,

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:57.380
the CEO will have no choice
 but to do as I wish.

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:01.340
I won't let him say anything about
killing Hiroki ever again.

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:05.930
Hiroki ran away because he was
 scared of crushing Satoru.

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:10.480
So if I crush Satoru instead,
he will surely come back to me.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:14.820
But if Hiroki still refuses...

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:23.320
I'll just have another mouth
to feed every day.

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:27.830
If Hiroki won't change his mind,
he can sit here like this.

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:31.830
That way, no one will ever
 tear us apart again.

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:36.840
So why are we even living together?

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:41.470
I mean... can't you meet me halfway?

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:44.600
We're gonna have to compromise here.

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:47.970
I wonder where the halfway point
 with Tsukasa might be...

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:52.980
I want to spend time with you.
Why do you always go drinking after work?

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:55.730
Okay! I won't go out drinking anymore.

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:58.780
So you have dinner, go to bed and
get up at 3:00 a.m., okay?

00:19:58.940 --> 00:19:59.940
3:00 a.m.?

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:03.030
Yeah. That's when you and I
can have some quality time, right?

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:06.120
We can go out on
early-morning dates together.

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:10.370
Tsukasa has no interest in finding
a halfway point with me.

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:12.620
Don't contradict me, Hiroki!

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:16.670
He thinks I'm supposed to
 just listen to everything he says.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:20.670
There's no other way
 but to crush Satoru.

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:23.180
But I don't want to crush Satoru.

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:27.470
Do I really have to listen to everything
 you say for us to be together?

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:30.810
But even if I were
 to stay with the Company,

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:34.150
Tsukasa is sure to one day
 become their prey.

00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:36.440
I want to protect him...

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:45.820
But even when he's right in front of
my eyes, I can't do anything to help him.

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:48.200
The Tsukasa I saw that day...

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:52.200
looked completely trapped.

00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:54.210
If we could just make a run for it,

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.080
why would I have crushed Mr. Hayashi?

00:20:57.790 --> 00:20:59.090
Did I run off...

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:02.590
when Tsukasa needed my help most?

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:07.720
Huh? A butterfly?

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:10.060
Wait, isn't this...?

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:13.180
Who's there?

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:15.600
It's the butterfly from the other day.

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:19.270
Someone is talking
to Meiling's butterfly.

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:23.780
Meiling, bring that person here.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:27.030
Katsuragi, stop the car!
We've got him!

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:34.250
We found you, Hiroki!

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:37.750
Satoru... Tsukasa. Why?

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:42.090
So that's it. It was that girl's image...

00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:44.220
You dare ask "why"?

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:48.840
Did you really think you could crush
Mr. Hayashi and get away with it?

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:50.010
What?

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:52.260
Don't play dumb, Hiroki.

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:56.390
Satoru knows all about
how you crushed Mr. Hayashi.

00:21:56.890 --> 00:21:59.100
What are you talking about, Tsukasa?

00:21:59.270 --> 00:22:00.770
Where are you hiding now?

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:03.190
If you won't tell us,
we'll search your memory.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:05.150
Shit. There's only one thing for it.

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:06.900
He's going to kick us out.

00:22:07.150 --> 00:22:08.660
Like hell he is!

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:12.660
What the...?

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:15.910
I upgraded to a new model!

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:55.050
Artist: Atsushi Kaneko
